+## 4. Coordinator-only commands
+These six are never dispatched as workers and get no `--unattended` mode. Their purpose is orchestration, a conversation with a person, or an outward action the user must authorize, which under this design belongs to the coordinator or to the person. Making them workers would remove their purpose (`INV-B:311`).
+
+| Command | Why it stays with the coordinator or the person | What the coordinator does instead | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `/sc:agent` | A whole-session controller that "owns the entire workflow", stops until the user describes a task, and keeps "the user out of the loop". That is the coordinator's role; two controllers would compete. | Plans and dispatches workers itself. | `cmd/agent.md:17,23,72`; `INV-A:36,90` |
+| `/sc:git` | Its job is git itself: most operations (commit, push, pull, branch, merge) mutate the repository and need the user's authorization in this repo, and destructive ones wait for confirmation. The read-only ones (`status`) give a worker nothing worth dispatching. | Runs git itself, only when the user asked; workers make no commits or pushes. | `cmd/git.md:14-17,90`; `.dev/orca-command-refactor/README.md:31`; `INV-A:49,91` |
+| `/sc:help` | Read-only listing printed to chat; writes nothing, so a worker would return nothing the coordinator can read. | Runs it in its own session when it needs the list. | `cmd/help.md:21,132`; `INV-A:50,92` |
+| `/sc:pm` | A competing always-on orchestrator that claims every session, delegates to every specialist, edits `CLAUDE.md` and overwrites single-owner memory keys. | Holds the plan and the memory itself. | `cmd/pm.md:12-17`; `sk/sc-pm-protocol/SKILL.md:48,52-54,56-84,158`; `cmd/save.md:44`; `INV-B:32,67-75,285` |
+| `/sc:spawn` | Decomposes work into Epic/Story/Task and delegates to other `/sc:*` commands, which is exactly the coordinator's Task DAG; it also has no output path and contradicts itself on whether it executes. | Builds the Task DAG with `task-create --deps` and ready waves (`CAPS:84-92`). | `cmd/spawn.md:28-36,140,192-210`; `INV-B:42,167-175,286` |
+| `/sc:swarm-wizard` | A Socratic `AskUserQuestion` interview plus an explicit go-ahead before a real-model run. | Dispatches a worker that runs `uv run superclaude swarm run ...` with explicit flags, which needs no wizard. | `sk/sc-swarm-wizard-protocol/SKILL.md:84,143-144`; `INV-B:44,187-195,287` |
+
+Two worker-capable commands are better used on the coordinator side, though they stay in section 3: `/sc:load` only loads context into the current session (`INV-B:65`), and `/sc:recommend` writes a prompt addressed to a person who pastes it (`INV-B:105`). `/sc:pr-submit` stays a worker candidate only if the user accepts open decision D3.
