+## 5. Standalone use without Orca keeps working unchanged
+A person who runs any `/sc:` command in a plain Claude session, inside or outside Orca, with or without Orca installed, must see exactly today's behaviour. This is a hard requirement on every phase.
+
+| ID | Requirement | Why | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| SA-1 | Without `--unattended`, every prompt, approval gate, default flag value, output path and outward default stays as it is today, including the auggie-review PR posting default and every `AskUserQuestion`. | The routing guide sends people to these commands with these behaviours today (for example `--interactive` controls on cleanup and improve, interactive suite selection on cli-eval). | `src/superclaude/core/HOW-WE-WORK.md:171,249,254` |
+| SA-2 | No command, skill or agent file runs an `orca` or `orca-ide` command, and none requires Orca to be installed or running. The only allowed mention of Orca in a changed command is as an example of a caller's question channel inside the contract file. | Commands run in other projects (`CLAUDE.md:74`); without Orca the calls fail with `runtime_unavailable` (`CAPS:147`). | `CAPS:145-149`; today's baseline: only `sk/ccsession-tag/` mentions Orca (section 1.2, E5) |
+| SA-3 | The worker contract and new report files are written only in unattended mode or when the caller passes the new output flag. A standalone default run writes the same files it writes today. | A new file appearing in a person's working tree is a visible change. | Section 3 rows that add a report path |
+| SA-4 | Command-file edits in Phases 1-3 are additive: a new `## Unattended mode` section and new flags. Existing lines change only where section 3 names a defect fix (roadmap and validate-roadmap drift, validate-tests target, adversarial and workflow contract gaps, explain tools, business-panel frontmatter, load usage line), and each such fix must keep the standalone behaviour or correct a documented defect. | Keeps the diff reviewable and SA-1 checkable. | Section 3 "Other required change" column |
