+| Name of the unattended switch | `--unattended`, `--worker`, `--orca`, `--non-interactive` | `--unattended` names the condition (no person), not a tool, so it stays meaningful for any caller (SA-2). `--non-interactive` reads as the opposite of the existing opt-in `--interactive` flags, which are already off by default (`INV-B:301`), so it would not signal the stronger rule (no gates, no outward defaults). |
