+## 1. Decision: Orca coordinates, commands stay the units of work
+
+### 1.1 The decision
+An Orca coordinator plans the work, creates Tasks, starts one worker per Task and reads each worker's report. Each IronClaude `/sc:` command stays a self-contained unit of work: one worker (a top-level Claude session in its own Orca terminal) runs one command and reports it with `worker_done`. Commands themselves contain no Orca calls. What changes in the commands is limited to the worker contract in section 2: a way to run without a person, a fixed report file, and a resume or safe re-run.
+
+### 1.2 Evidence for the decision
+| # | Claim | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| E1 | Orca's model is a coordinator that starts workers; a Run does not schedule work itself, so something above the commands must do the planning. | `[G]` lines 51-52, quoted at `CAPS:92`; ready-wave pattern at `CAPS:86` |
+| E2 | A worker is already a top-level Claude session, so a command run by a worker has the same tools as a command a person runs. | `CAPS:161` (`[H:worker-start]` line 38, `--agent claude`); `.dev/evals/ccsession-orca-e2e-20261026/EVIDENCE.md:45` (worker reached `state: ready, stage: input_accepted` and answered) |
+| E3 | It has worked before: in the codegraph planning run, Orca workers invoked `/sc:adversarial`, and that work landed as PR #329. | `.dev/codegraph-migration/orchestration/README.md:31,33`; `.dev/orca-command-refactor/README.md:12`; return contract `invocation_method: "skill-direct"` at `.dev/codegraph-migration/decisions/P3-command-set/adversarial/return-contract.yaml:10` |
+| E4 | Commands keep their own internal fan-out. Agent-tool subagents inside a worker are not Orca workers and are not counted by Orca's nesting limit. | `CAPS:155` (`nested-worker-depth.js:7-11,18-22`); fan-out per command in column (c) of `INV-A:35-55` and `INV-B:31-52` |
+| E5 | Nothing has to be removed: no command, skill, agent or core file calls Orca today. The only Orca-aware primitive is the `ccsession-tag` launcher. | `grep -rlni orca src/superclaude/{commands,skills,core,agents}` (run 2026-11-02) lists only files under `sk/ccsession-tag/`; `grep -ci orca src/superclaude/core/HOW-WE-WORK.md` printed `0` |
+| E6 | The gaps the inventories found are person-blocking gates, missing report files, interface drift and shared-state clobbering. None is fixed by making commands call Orca, and all must be fixed under either design. | `INV-A:76-83`, `INV-A:94-98`; `INV-B:289-299` |
