+### 2.3 What the coordinator owes each worker
+The contract only works if the brief carries what the command would otherwise ask a person. For each Task the coordinator's brief states: the exact command line including `--unattended` and every flag section 3 lists as required; a `--contract <base>/<dispatch_id>/worker-contract.yaml` path and output paths under the same `<base>/<dispatch_id>/`, with the instruction that the worker replaces `<dispatch_id>` with the Dispatch ID from its preamble (WC-4, WC-6), so the coordinator knows the contract path as soon as `worker-start` returns the Dispatch ID; the command's own output flag pointing under that base (`--output <base>/<dispatch_id>/` or `--output <base>/<dispatch_id>/<file>`, and `--output-dir <base>/<dispatch_id>/` for troubleshoot, `cmd/troubleshoot.md:56`), so no output path is timestamped or defaulted; which outward actions, if any, are authorized (WC-9); the worktree placement (`CAPS:115`); and the **worker-session block**, copied verbatim from the contract file's brief template. The block is the only carrier of the worker-session duties, because Orca's own preamble covers heartbeats, `ask`, `check` and `worker_done` but none of this contract's additions, and the command's Unattended section is read only after the command started. It says, in this order: (1) replace `<dispatch_id>` in every path with the Dispatch ID from your preamble (WC-6); (2) invoke the command with the `Skill` tool as `sc:<name>` (or as the slash command) from this top-level session; never by reading its file and carrying out its steps, never inside an Agent-tool subagent (WC-7); (3) send a heartbeat immediately before and after each Agent-tool call the command makes, and never send lifecycle messages from a subagent (WC-7, WC-10); (4) if the worker contract ends `blocked`, follow WC-3 (one `ask` per gate, only for a gate whose section 3 row names the answering flag, re-run with the same `--contract`); (5) send `worker_done` exactly once with `--outcome` per WC-5 and `--report-path` set to the `--contract` path (WC-4, WC-5); (6) run `check` at checkpoints and once before `worker_done` (WC-12). After `worker_done`, the coordinator opens the report file, then releases or reuses the worker (`CAPS:107-113`).
