+## 7. Acceptance checks per phase
+Run from the repo root. `ORCA` means `orca-ide` outside an Orca terminal and `orca` inside one (`CAPS:145`). A phase passes only when every check in its block and every common check passes.
+
+### 7.1 Common checks (every phase)
+| ID | Check | Pass condition |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-C1 | The command in the code block below this table (kept out of the table so no `\|` escape can be copied by mistake). It matches any word starting with `orca`, case-insensitive, so every Orca invocation form is caught: `orca` and `orca-ide` with any subcommand (`skills get`, `status`, `open`, `orchestration`, ...), `ORCA` placeholders and `"$ORCA" ...`; this is exact for SA-2, which forbids any Orca mention outside core. It scans commands, skills and agents only, not `src/superclaude/core/`, where SA-2 allows Orca text. | prints nothing (SA-2, WC-8). Baseline on 2026-11-08 in this worktree: prints nothing; on a sample file it matched `"$ORCA" orchestration task-create`, `orca-ide skills get orchestration` and `orca status --json` |
+| AC-C2 | `make verify-sync` | exits 0 (SA-5) |
+| AC-C3 | Before the phase starts, save `uv run pytest tests/skills/ -q -rf` output as the baseline; after the phase, run it again | no test that passed in the baseline fails; new tests pass. A clean suite is not assumed (an earlier run saw pre-existing failures, `.dev/codegraph-migration/orchestration/README.md:42`) |
+| AC-C4 | `git diff --cached --name-only \| grep '^\.claude/' \| grep -v '^\.claude/settings\.json$'` | prints nothing (`CLAUDE.md:16`) |
+| AC-C5 | For every command file the phase edits without a named defect fix (SA-4): the AC-C5 command below, with `<name>` replaced. It compares word by word, so flags inserted between existing words of the Usage or `argument-hint:` line show as additions only, and it drops only the `--- a/...` file header, so a removed markdown bullet (`- item`, shown as `-- item`) is still printed. | prints nothing: no existing word was removed or changed |
+
+AC-C1 command:
+
+```sh
+grep -rniE '\borca' \
+  src/superclaude/commands src/superclaude/skills src/superclaude/agents \
+  | grep -v '^src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/'
+```
+
+AC-C5 command (also used by AC-0.3 with the routing-guide path):
+
+```sh
+git diff -U0 --word-diff=porcelain master...HEAD -- src/superclaude/commands/<name>.md \
+  | grep -vE '^--- (a/|/dev/null)' | grep -E '^-'
+```
+
+Both forms were tested on 2026-11-08 in a scratch repository: inserting `[--unattended] [--contract <path>]` between words of an `argument-hint:` line and at the end of a Usage line printed nothing; deleting one word printed it; deleting a `- bullet one` line printed `-- bullet one`, which the old `grep -E '^-[^-]'` filter missed.
