+### 7.2 Live worker check (used by P0-P4)
+For each command under test, the coordinator runs the steps below. Live-check workers run one at a time per worktree (or each in its own worktree), so step 6 can attribute every change to the worker under test. `<scratch>` is a directory outside the worktree.
+
+Step P (installed copy). `cmp` each file the worker will load against its branch source: `~/.claude/commands/sc/<name>.md` against `src/superclaude/commands/<name>.md`, every file of each skill the command names under `~/.claude/skills/<skill>/` against `src/superclaude/skills/<skill>/`, and from P1 on `~/.claude/WORKER-CONTRACT.md` against `src/superclaude/core/WORKER-CONTRACT.md`; if the worktree has a project `.claude/commands/sc/<name>.md` or `.claude/skills/<skill>/`, those must match too. **Pass:** every `cmp` exits 0. If any differs, install the branch as the user chose under D6 (for D6 (a), `uv run superclaude install --force` from the branch checkout) and repeat; a live check run without matching copies is not a result, pass or fail.
+
+Step 0: `touch <scratch>/start.stamp` and `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all > <scratch>/before.txt`.
+1. `ORCA orchestration task-create --spec "<brief per section 2.3, including the worker-session block>" --json`, then `ORCA orchestration worker-start --task <task_id> --worktree current --agent claude --json`. **Pass:** exit 0 and `state: ready` (`CAPS:46`).
+2. While it runs, `ORCA orchestration worker-show --dispatch <dispatch_id> --json` at least once per 5 minutes. **Pass:** `observation.agentWait` is never non-null (a non-null value means the worker is parked on a prompt only a person can answer, `[H:worker-show]` Notes).
+3. `ORCA orchestration check --wait --types "worker_done,escalation,question" --timeout-ms 900000 --json` until `worker_done` arrives. The coordinator answers each `question` with `ORCA orchestration reply --id <msg_id> --body "<text>"` by the check's own rule: in a gate-trigger run (AC-2.2) the body is exactly `NO ANSWER: gate-trigger test`, which names no usable value, so WC-3 (4) makes the worker keep and report the blocked contract; in every other run a `question` already fails the check (the brief must carry every value), and the coordinator replies with the same text so the worker settles. **Pass:** exactly one `worker_done`; no `question` outside a gate-trigger run; its `--outcome` matches the worker contract's `status` under WC-5; its report path is the `--contract` path from the brief with `<dispatch_id>` replaced by this Dispatch's ID (WC-4, section 2.3). Before P1 (AC-0.4) the report path is instead the command's existing report file named in section 3.1.
