+6. `find . -path ./.git -prune -o -type f -newer <scratch>/start.stamp -print` (every file created or modified since step 0, tracked, untracked or gitignored, including a file that was already modified before), and `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all > <scratch>/after.txt; comm -13 <(sort <scratch>/before.txt) <(sort <scratch>/after.txt)` (new status lines, which also shows deletions). **Pass:** every path either command prints is under the brief's `<base>/<dispatch_id>/` location, is one of the command's documented artifacts, or is under `.codegraph/` (the gitignored code-graph index, `.gitignore:262`, which its file watcher updates). A file that was dirty before step 0 and not touched again is not printed, so a worktree that was dirty before the worker started does not fail the check.
